  "notes": "USAGE: {反抗|はんこう} refers to opposing or resisting authority. It's commonly used when discussing adolescent rebellion or resistance to rules.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{反抗|はんこう}する (to rebel, to resist)\n・〜に{反抗|はんこう}する (to rebel against ~)\n・{反抗|はんこう}{的|てき} (rebellious, defiant)\n・{反抗|はんこう}{心|しん} (rebellious spirit)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n・{反抗|はんこう}{期|き} (rebellious phase/period - esp. adolescence)\n・{反抗|はんこう}{心|しん} (spirit of rebellion)\n・{反抗|はんこう}{的|てき}な{態度|たいど} (defiant attitude)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{抵抗|ていこう} - resistance (physical or metaphorical)\n・{反対|はんたい} - opposition (to an idea/plan)\n・{反発|はんぱつ} - opposition, backlash",
